From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:04:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 66/75] driver core: fw_devlink: don't report refused
 sync_state()-only links

When a supplier device appears after its consumer has bound,
fw_devlink_create_devlink() asks for a sync_state()-only link, which
device_link_add() refuses by design: such a link only holds the
supplier's sync_state() back until the consumer probes, and that has
already happened. The refusal is still reported as an error.

On a Radxa Dragon Q8B the PMIC GLINK device binds early, and each USB
controller, PHY and SBU mux that its connector nodes reference then
logs one of these:

  qcom_pmic_glink pmic-glink: Failed to create device link (0x180) with
    supplier a600000.usb for /pmic-glink/connector@0

Report that case at debug level and keep the error for real failures.
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
index 4d02668..1ff8363 100644
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -2237,8 +2237,18 @@ static int fw_devlink_create_devlink(struct device *con,
 		}
 
 		if (con != sup_dev && !device_link_add(con, sup_dev, flags)) {
-			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
-				flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
+			/*
+			 * device_link_add() refuses a sync_state()-only link
+			 * once the consumer has probed: the link would only
+			 * have held the supplier's sync_state() back until then.
+			 */
+			if (flags & DL_FLAG_SYNC_STATE_ONLY &&
+			    con->links.status == DL_DEV_DRIVER_BOUND)
+				dev_dbg(con, "Not linking %s for %pfwf: consumer already bound\n",
+					dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
+			else
+				dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
+					flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 		}
 
